> [!WARNING]
> **`grpc_server.await` blocks the WAL drain when `axum::serve` returns an error**
>
> <sub>F2 · Warning · correctness</sub>

`run_grpc_server` only returns once `serve_with_shutdown` sees a shutdown signal, so when `axum::serve` returns `Err` (an accept error) without one, the join at `main.rs:3216` never completes: main never reaches the drain, `flush_wal_to_object_store` and the `Ingest server failed` line at `main.rs:3278` never run, and the task lingers until someone sends SIGTERM. Before this hunk the same failure drained the WAL and called `exit(1)`.

```
Bound the join: abort the gRPC task when `serve_result.is_err()`, or wrap `grpc_server.await` in `tokio::time::timeout(drain_deadline, ...)` so a stalled gRPC server cannot hold the drain.
```

```suggestion
    // Its exports must land in the WAL before the drain below reads it. A failed
    // `axum::serve` returns without a shutdown signal, and the gRPC server only
    // stops on one, so do not block the drain on it.
    if let Some(grpc_server) = grpc_server {
        if serve_result.is_err() {
            grpc_server.abort();
        } else {
            drop(grpc_server.await);
        }
    }
```
